# Design documents in temp/

Use `temp/` for throwaway HTML mockups that explore UI before (or
alongside) React implementation. Everything under `temp/` is gitignored —
never stage or commit these files.

## When to create one

- Proposing a new screen, layout, or visual treatment.
- Comparing two or more UI options side by side.
- Sharing a self-contained preview the user can open in a browser.

## File conventions

- **Location:** `temp/<descriptive-name>.html` (kebab-case, e.g.
  `jobs-screen-layout.html`).
- **Self-contained:** Single HTML file with inline `<style>` (and minimal
  inline `<script>` only when interaction helps the mockup). Do not import
  from `src/` — duplicate what you need so the file opens standalone.
- **Title:** Set `<title>` and a visible `<h1>` or header comment at the top
  stating purpose, date, and what is in/out of scope.

## Match the app look

Mirror the dark theme from `src/styles/tokens.css`:

- Background `#0a0c12`, text `#f6f6f6`, muted `rgba(255,255,255,0.55)`
- Accent / progress `#58a6ff`, focus `#8ab7ff`
- Surfaces: flat blue-tinted fills, no 1px borders; use `--radius-sm/md/lg`
  (4 / 6 / 8px)
- Sidebar width 56px, title bar ~34px when mocking shell chrome

Player chrome may follow the Soia reference style (bottom gradient bar,
custom seek, icon transport buttons) — see `CONTEXT.md` and
`src/styles/player.css`.

## Content guidelines

- Use realistic placeholder copy and sample data, not lorem ipsum walls.
- Annotate non-obvious choices with HTML comments (`<!-- why: … -->`).
- Prefer static markup; fake interactivity with CSS or a few lines of JS
  only when it clarifies the design.
- If multiple variants, use separate files or clearly labeled sections in
  one file — do not mix unrelated experiments without labels.

## After the mockup

- Implement approved ideas in `src/components/` and `src/styles/`.
- Delete or overwrite obsolete mockups in `temp/`; they are not archived in
  git.
